Statistically, the measurement to extract the \(\mathsf{J}/\psi\) polarization parameters from the dataset is point estimation.

In this study, maximum likelihood estimation is applied to extract parameters of \(\mathsf{J}/\psi\) polarization. The negative log-likelihood is calculated based on the probability density function, spatial distribution of positron decay from \(\mathsf{J}/\psi\) and reconstruction efficiency \(\epsilon(\cos\theta,\phi)\):

\[\mathsf{P}(\cos\theta,\phi|\lambda_{\theta},\lambda_{\phi},\lambda_{\theta \phi})=\frac{\partial^{2}\mathsf{N}}{\partial\cos\theta\partial\phi}(\cos \theta,\phi|\lambda_{\theta},\lambda_{\phi},\lambda_{\theta\phi})*\epsilon( \cos\theta,\phi). \tag{4.2}\]

